                       interprets the _a_d_d_r argument as the TID of a proc.

                 sshhooww rreeggiisstteerrss [//uu]
                       Display the register set.  If the //uu modifier is speci‐
                       fied, it displays user registers (or the currently
                       saved registers) instead of the kernel's.  Note: The //uu
                       modifier is not supported on every machine, in which
                       case incorrect information may be displayed.

                 sshhooww rroouuttee _a_d_d_r
                       Prints the _s_t_r_u_c_t _r_t_e_n_t_r_y at _a_d_d_r.

                 sshhooww ssoocckkeett _a_d_d_r
                       Prints the _s_t_r_u_c_t _s_o_c_k_e_t at _a_d_d_r.  If the socket is
                       spliced, the _s_t_r_u_c_t _s_o_s_p_l_i_c_e associated with the socket
                       is printed as well.

                 sshhooww ssttrruucctt _n_a_m_e [addr]
                       Prints the content of the memory at _a_d_d_r as a struct
                       _n_a_m_e.  Nested structures and bit fields are not
                       printed.  Character arrays are printed as bytes.

                 sshhooww sswwaapp
                       Prints a detailed list of all swaps.

                 sshhooww ttddbb [//ff] _a_d_d_r
                       Prints the _s_t_r_u_c_t _t_d_b at _a_d_d_r.  If the //ff modifier is
