                 sshhooww aallll pprrooccss [//aannooww]
                       Display information on all processes.

                       //nn   (Default) Show process information in a ps(1)-like
                            format.  Information printed includes process ID,
                            thread ID, parent process ID, UID, process status,
                            process flags, process wait channel message and
                            process command name.
                       //aa   Shows the kernel virtual addresses of each
                            process' proc structure, u-area, and vmspace
                            structure.  The vmspace address is also the ad‐
                            dress of the process' vm_map structure and can be
                            used in the sshhooww mmaapp command.
                       //oo   Shows non-idle threads that were on CPU when ddb
                            was entered.  Information printed includes thread
                            ID, process ID, UID, process flags, thread flags,
                            current CPU, and command name.
                       //ww   Shows each thread's ID, command, process group,
                            wait channel address, and wait channel message.

                 sshhooww aallll bbuuffss [//ff]
                       Display information about all buffers in the system.

                       //ff   For each buffer, print a more detailed output.
                            See the sshhooww bbuuff command for more information.

